<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sirmium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sirmium was a Roman city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, today Sremska Mitrovica in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>. In the late 3rd and 4th centuries it was one of the imperial residences of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetrarchy">Tetrarchy</a> and the birthplace of several emperors, among them Probus. Later held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a>, it was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> in 582 after a long siege.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sirmium.jpg" alt="Sirmium" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: mediaportal.vojvodina.gov.rs · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carska_palata_Sirmijum1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
